# Python bytecode — regenerated on every run, never useful in git.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local virtualenv created by init.sh (~1.6 GB).
.venv/

# pytest scratch
.pytest_cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED: chroma_db/ and scraper/normalized/
#
# These are committed on purpose and the deployment depends on it. Render has an
# ephemeral filesystem and there is no database server, so the vector store and
# the images ship *inside the build*. Production proves it: GET / returns
# {"status":"ok","indexed":78}, and that 78 is read from the committed chroma_db.
#
# Ignoring or removing them would leave the deployed API with an empty index and
# no images to serve, with no error to explain why.
#
# Known wart: opening the Chroma client appends a row to the internal
# `acquire_write` lock table, so chroma_db/chroma.sqlite3 shows as modified after
# any run. Verified harmless — all 156 embedding rows and every other table are
# identical; only that lock table differs. Discard it before committing:
#     git checkout -- chroma_db/
# Only commit chroma_db/ when you have actually re-vectorized.
